WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.047
Fluent A I links lessons with learner memory.
This demo uses scripted model responses.

2
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:13.176
A temporary learner profile opens a past-tense
lesson, with a visible selection reason.

3
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:24.464
The learner answers six questions, mixing
vocabulary, sentences, and translation. One
answer is deliberately wrong so we can follow
the feedback.

4
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:32.175
Five answers are correct. The mistake gets
feedback and becomes a scheduled review item.

5
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.227
Back home, the score, experience points, and
review queue reflect the completed lesson.

6
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.021
Now text practice picks up the same past-tense
topic.

7
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.947
A short Spanish reply receives feedback and a
follow-up prompt.

8
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.613
A second reply continues the exchange. These are
scripted responses, exercising the app's
practice workflow.

9
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.675
The memory inspector exposes the saved profile,
skills, topic scores, and mistakes.

10
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:20.176
Reloading keeps the lesson result and review
queue. This demonstrates saved progress across
the workflow; live voice and model quality are
outside this recording.
